eak equities markets. April Comex gold settled up 0.2%, at $1,396.10/oz. Crude-oil futures settled higher, helped by political unrest in Bahrain and some bargain-hunting after the prior session's sharp drop, but their advance cooled after remarks about Japan's nuclear crisis from a European Union energy official; April Nymex crude rose 0.8% to settle at $97.98/bbl. (lucy.craymer@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2155 GMT [Dow Jones] The AUD/USD needs a circuit breaker or else the pair could fall much further, says CBA \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Joseph Capurso. He highlights two possible circuit breakers as an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the USD/JPY by the MOF, or any calming words from the head of the International Atomic Energy Agency. If neither of those events play out, the AUD/USD cross will tumble. "It could continue to get quite messy." The AUD/USD cross is at 0.9782. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2140 GMT [Dow Jones] The NZD/USD cross takes a tumble as the USD plummets against the JPY. The Kiwi is falling against all crosses, hitting 2-year lows against JPY. The NZD/JPY is at 55.43 after dipping to 54.985. "Markets are more than erratic, pricing action has gone insane" and things are "in a type of free fall," says ANZ senior dealer Alex Sinton. The NZD/USD dipped to 0.7136, its lowest level since early September, but has bounced back to 0.7173. He says the bias, however, is to the downside with key support at 0.7108. (rebecca.howard@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2132 GMT [Dow Jones] The AUD/USD is at risk of collapsing as long as USD/JPY continues to slide, says RBS \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Greg Gibbs. He says the AUD move so far is benign given there is no real clear support base at current levels. The AUD/USD cross is at 0.9758, about a four month low. For USD/JPY, doesn't expect any let up in the selling. Pair last 97.51, around record lows. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \