\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Major  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Rangebound Amid Relative Calm\b0\par\par\uc2 876 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 13:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 --Some respite in wider markets as Nikkei rises\par \par \uc2 --Underlying uncertainty around Japan still key\par \par \uc2 --Reports of some yen repatriation flows\par \par \uc2 --News surrounding euro seen as negative\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Siva Sithraputhran \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The euro took in its stride a ratings downgrade of Portugal overnight but attempts to push it past the $1.40 level against the dollar are proving difficult, while the yen remained steady as some semblance of normality returned to financial markets after share prices in Tokyo recovered some of their losses since the start of the week.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That said, the outlook in Japan is still marked by uncertainty after the earthquake Friday and news on the escalating nuclear crisis in the country continues to keep investors on edge.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "My suspicion is that this is temporary respite," Neil Mellor, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Bank of New York Mellon said of the relative calm in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  too noted some stabilization in confidence levels overall, but said that although the euro is finding decent support, the news surrounding the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is still negative after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  downgraded Portugal by two notches to A3, making it hard for the single \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to pierce through $1.40.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Some of the shine has also been taken off the agreement made at the EU Summit and the Ecofin meeting, with Trichet criticizing the agreement for dealing with countries that have high debt levels as not being tough enough," they said in a note to clients, adding that the euro may dip towards $1.3860.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mellor at Bank of New York Mellon said he expects the dollar to emerge as the safe haven of choice despite the fiscal and monetary policy troubles in the U.S.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As the yen continues to find safe-haven buying demand, it has been able to rise against the euro, he added\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, in Japan, a plan to drop water on part of the crippled Fukushima Daiichi nuclear plant from helicopters has been abandoned for the day due to excessive radiation levels. Preparations for a new attempt are now underway, said Japan's Chief Cabinet Secretary Yukio Edano.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The difficulty in bringing the nuclear situation under control is continuing to weigh on sentiment, while the opposing forces of expected yen repatriation and the threat of Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  still hold sway, keeping the yen rangebound against the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays Capital\f28 \uc2 \f2  said that some repatriation my already be occurring and is likely to continue over the coming weeks but Bank of New York Mellon's Mellor said such evidence is "still very limited" and remains "the big unknown."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Sterling is little changed after mixed unemployment data. The number of people claiming unemployment benefit in the U.K. fell unexpectedly in February, to its lowest level in two years but the wider international measure of unemployment rose 27,000 in the three months to the end of January, pushing the headline rate up to 8.0%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Elsewhere, the Norwegian krone is holding steady, with the markets expecting the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  to keep rates on hold at 2% later Wednesday. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Norges Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  rate decision is at 1300 GMT and a news conference will follow the event at 1345 GMT.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts at Credit Agricole said they expect a no-change decision as the krone has weakened alongside a drop in oil prices. However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's comments at the ensuing news conference will be watched closely. If it plays down inflation risks, the krone may weaken, said anlysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 UBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro was trading at $1.3932 from $1.4000 late Tuesday in New York, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y80.70 from Y80.72, while the euro was at Y112.48 from Y114.22. The U.K. pound was at $1.6063 from $1.6088. The dollar was at CHF0.9167 from CHF0.9164.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the U.S. dollar against a trade-weighted basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , was at 76.551 from 76.343.\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  spot:       EUR/USD    USD/JPY    GBP/USD    USD/CHF \par  \par Spot 1129 GMT     1.3944     80.69      1.6073     0.9163 \par 3 Day Trend       Range      Bearish    Range      Bearish \par Weekly Trend      Bullish    Bearish    Bearish    Bearish \par 200 day ma        1.3464     84.43      1.5786     0.9873 \par 3rd Resistance    1.4036     81.55      1.6199     0.9235 \par 2nd Resistance    1.4013     81.22      1.6140     0.9204 \par 1st Resistance    1.4001     80.98      1.6125     0.9198 \par Pivot*            1.3955     81.13      1.6084     0.9185 \par 1st Support       1.3915     80.60      1.6050  