\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 871 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 10:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: JAPAN FACES SETBACKS FIGHT TO CONTROL NUCLEAR REACTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan faced new setbacks in its struggle to tame a quake-ravaged nuclear complex as a fresh fire broke out there early Wednesday, workers were temporarily moved to safer locations, and new threats emerged in previously unaffected parts of the plant. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ CONTINUES POST-QUAKE INJECTION, OFFERS Y13.8 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan Wednesday continued to try to calm concern about the impact of the earthquake and nuclear power crisis on the economy, offering to inject another Y13.8 trillion in short-term funds into the money market. (published 0809 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN EDANO: RADIATION LEVELS SPIKED AT NUCLEAR PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Wednesday that radiation levels had again spiked at a smoking, quake-hit nuclear plant, but said there was no need to expand the evacuation area around the plant based on current data. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN DPJ OFFICIAL: NODA SAYS TO PAY ATTENTION TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said he will pay attention to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, according to a lawmaker who met Noda earlier Wednesday. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par INTERVIEW: MOODY'S: WOULD WANT TO ANTICIPATE JAPAN DEBT TIPPING POINT WITH RATINGS ACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service would want to anticipate any shift in investor sentiment toward Japanese government debt, but it would have taken "more forceful" ratings action in February had it believed that a deterioration in borrowing conditions was imminent, a senior analyst at the credit rating agency said. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par HIGH COUPON HELPS 20-YEAR JGB AUCTION DESPITE QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An attractive coupon succeeded in drawing investor demand for 20-year Japanese government bonds at an auction Wednesday, despite uncertainties over the economic and financial impact of the country's unprecedented natural and nuclear disasters. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par US, EUROPE UNLIKELY TO AID \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -FORMER FED OFFICIALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. and Europe are unlikely to coordinate a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to aid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's battered economy because the country currently has enough cash firepower, former U.S. Federal Reserve officials say. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par MOODY'S DOWNGRADES PORTUGAL; PM WARNS POLITICAL CRISIS A THREAT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Portugal faced further pressure late Tuesday after \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2  downgraded its long-term government bond ratings ahead of a key debt sale, and amid growing fears a political crisis is brewing in the country. (published 2310 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPE FEB NEW CAR REGISTRATIONS +1.4% ON YR AT 1.01M -ACEA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New car registrations in Europe increased 1.4% in February to 1.01 million vehicles, the European Automobile Manufacturers' Association, or ACEA, said Tuesday. (published 0708 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FORMER US FED GOV MISHKIN SAYS END OF QE IS A NON-ISSUE FOR TREASURYS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Former Governor of the U.S. Federal Reserve Rick Mishkin said Wednesday the end of the U.S. Treasury's US$600 billion government bond purchase program in June is unlikely to have a significant impact on long-term bond yields. (published 0442 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOK GOVERNOR: PRICE STABILITY GREATEST CHALLENGE FOR KOREA ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea Governor Kim Choong-soo said Wednesday price stability is the greatest challenge facing the country's economy, suggesting that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue its monetary tightening to curb rising inflation pressure. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA JOBLESS RATE AT YEAR-HIGH IN FEB; APRIL RATE HIKE UNLIKELY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's unemployment rate rose for a third straight month to hit a year-high in February amid concerns that rising inflation could eventually dent the economic recovery. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA JANUARY WESTPAC-MI LEADING INDEX +3.5% ANNUALIZED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A leading index of the Australian economy released Wednesday grew at an annualized rate of 3.5% in January, down from growth of 4.6% in December, as the impact of natural disasters in Queensland weighed on forecasts. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NIGERIA FOREIGN MINISTER: PLAN TO EXPAND CRUDE OUTPUT CAPACITY TO 4M BARRELS/DAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nigeria plans to increase its crude oil output capacity to 4 million barrels a day, Foreign Minister Henry Odein Ajumogobia said Wednesday. (published 0735 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN SCOUTING FOR LNG SUPPLIES; MAY BUY EXTRA 5 MLN TONS/YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese buyers have begun negotiations for more short and longer-term supplies of liquefied natural gas, as energy markets from Asia to Europe brace for higher gas prices following last week's massive earthquake in Japan. (published 0802 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIAN HOUSING STARTS FALL 5.3% IN 4Q VS 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The total number of houses and apartments that started construction in Australia in the fourth quarter of 2010 fell 5.3% to a seasonally adjusted 37,897 from the third quarter. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOVERNOR: 1Q GROWTH MAY REACH 6.6% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia Deputy Gov. Hartadi Sarwono Wednesday said the domestic economy may grow 6.6% in the first quarter from a year earlier. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par PREVIEW: HK DECEMBER-FEBRUARY JOBLESS RATE LIKELY UNCHANGED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's unemployment rate was likely unchanged in the three months ended Feb. 28 as the strength of the local economy continued to support the job market. (published 0511 GMT) [ 16-03-11 0903GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110316e73g000o5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
