\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For March 16\b0\par\par\uc2 2,111 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 08:02\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par WSJ: JAPAN FACES SETBACKS FIGHT TO CONTROL NUCLEAR REACTORS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan faced new setbacks in its struggle to tame a quake-ravaged nuclear complex as a fresh fire broke out there early Wednesday, workers were temporarily moved to safer locations, and new threats emerged in previously unaffected parts of the plant. (published 0555 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: JAPAN EDANO: RADIATION LEVELS SPIKED AT NUCLEAR PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Wednesday that radiation levels had again spiked at a smoking, quake-hit nuclear plant, but said there was no need to expand the evacuation area around the plant based on current data. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN DPJ OFFICIAL: NODA SAYS TO PAY ATTENTION TO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda said he will pay attention to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market, according to a lawmaker who met Noda earlier Wednesday. (published 0303 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: BOJ OFFERS Y5.5 TLN VIA SAME-DAY, REPO \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATIONS\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 The Bank of Japan Wednesday continued to try to calm worries about the impact of the devastating earthquake and nuclear power crisis on the economy, offering to inject another Y5.5 trillion in emergency funds into the money market. (published 0201 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INTERVIEW: MOODY'S: WOULD WANT TO ANTICIPATE JAPAN DEBT TIPPING POINT WITH RATINGS ACTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Moody's Investors Service would want to anticipate any shift in investor sentiment toward Japanese government debt, but it would have taken "more forceful" ratings action in February had it believed that a deterioration in borrowing conditions was imminent, a senior analyst at the credit rating agency said. (published 0202 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: INTERVIEW: ABERDEEN SAYS JAPAN REBUILD CAPEX WON'T BE GOOD FOR BONDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The massive amount of government expenditure needed to pay for the rebuilding effort in Japan will be a net negative on Japan's bond market, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Aberdeen Asset Management PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's Global Head of Fixed Income Paul Griffiths said Wednesday. (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: HIGH COUPON HELPS 20-YEAR JGB AUCTION DESPITE QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An attractive coupon succeeded in drawing investor demand for 20-year Japanese government bonds at an auction Wednesday, despite uncertainties over the economic and financial impact of the country's unprecedented natural and nuclear disasters. (published 0517 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par US, EUROPE UNLIKELY TO AID \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN FOREX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -FORMER FED OFFICIALS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. and Europe are unlikely to coordinate a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to aid \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's battered economy because the country currently has enough cash firepower, former U.S. Federal Reserve officials say. (published 0215 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOK GOVERNOR: PRICE STABILITY GREATEST CHALLENGE FOR KOREA ECONOMY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Korea Governor Kim Choong-soo said Wednesday price stability is the greatest challenge facing the country's economy, suggesting that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will continue its monetary tightening to curb rising inflation pressure. (published 0345 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: KOREA JOBLESS RATE AT YEAR-HIGH IN FEB; APRIL RATE HIKE UNLIKELY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's unemployment rate rose for a third straight month to hit a year-high in February amid concerns that rising inflation could eventually dent the economic recovery. (published 0305 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA JANUARY WESTPAC-MI LEADING INDEX +3.5% ANNUALIZED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A leading index of the Australian economy released Wednesday grew at an annualized rate of 3.5% in January, down from growth of 4.6% in December, as the impact of natural disasters in Queensland weighed on forecasts. (published 2330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIAN HOUSING STARTS FALL 5.3% IN 4Q VS 3Q \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The total number of houses and apartments that started construction in Australia in the fourth quarter of 2010 fell 5.3% to a seasonally adjusted 37,897 from the third quarter. (published 0031 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOVERNOR: 1Q GROWTH MAY REACH 6.6% ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia Deputy Gov. Hartadi Sarwono Wednesday said the domestic economy may grow 6.6% in the first quarter from a year earlier. (published 0619 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOVERNOR: IMPACT OF JAPAN QUAKE ON RUPIAH TO BE TEMPORARY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The impact on the Indonesian rupiah of the devastating natural disasters that have struck Japan will likely be temporary, a Bank Indonesia official said Wednesday. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA DEPUTY GOVERNOR: BASE EFFECT COULD KEEP MARCH ON-YEAR INFLATION HIGH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Indonesia expects on-year inflation to remain high in March given last year's low base of comparison, a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  official said Wednesday. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: WHOLE-MILK POWDER PRICES DOWN 11.4% IN FONTERRA AUCTION AS GLOBAL UNCERTAINTY WEIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Milk prices eased in Fonterra Co-Operative Group Ltd.'s auction early Wednesday morning, hurt by global uncertainty, in particular after Japan's devastating earthquake and tsunami. (published 0143 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PREVIEW: HK DECEMBER-FEBRUARY JOBLESS RATE LIKELY UNCHANGED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Hong Kong's unemployment rate was likely unchanged in the three months ended Feb. 28 as the strength of the local economy continued to support the job market. (published 0511 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOKYO SHARES END UP 5.7%, PARTIALLY REPAIRING PRIOR DAY'S LOSSES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tokyo shares clawed back some ground Wednesday, reversing a portion of the prior day's selloff, as bargain-hunting by hedge and other funds overcame jitters over Japan's still-unstable nuclear situation. (published 0650 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par TOYOTA: TO RESUME SEVEN DOMESTIC AUTO PART PLANTS FOR DOMESTIC MARKET FROM THURSDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Toyota Motor Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday that it will resume production of replacement parts at seven plants in Japan to supply for the domestic market. (published 0644 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINA MOBILE 2010 NET PROFIT RISES 3.9%, BUT COMPETITION WEIGHS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Mobile Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's biggest wireless operator by subscribers, said Wednesday its net profit rose 3.9% last year, as tougher competition and additions of low-income mobile subscribers in rural areas balanced out growth in the company's third-generation wireless business. (published 0630 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIAN FINANCIAL FIRMS NOT EVACUATING STAFF FROM JAPAN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian financial firms aren't evacuating staff from Tokyo despite concerns about aftershocks and potential radiation exposure in the city. (published 0330 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par RIO TINTO ACCEPTANCES FOR RIVERSDALE MINING BID RISE TO 30.59% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's offer for Africa-focused coal producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riversdale Mining Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . continues to slowly draw acceptances since the bid was raised, taking it to more than 30% of the voting rights, the company said Wednesday. (published 2249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: SINGAPORE EXCHANGE: TO INTRODUCE INITIAL AND INTERMEDIATE PRICE LIMITS ON NIKKEI FUTURES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Exchange Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it will add initial and intermediate price limits on SGX Nikkei futures contracts, starting from the open of European trading Wednesday. (published 0611 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREAT WALL MOTOR: HOPE TO START CHINA LISTING PROCESS AS EARLY AS SEPTEMBER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese car maker Great Wall Motor Co. said Wednesday it hopes to start its initial public offering of A shares ahead of a listing in China as early as September, once regulators approve the deal. (published 0440 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BILLABONG CUTS FY PROFIT VIEW, COULD BE AS MUCH AS 6% DOWN ON YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Billabong International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Wednesday downgraded full-year net profit after the earthquake and tsunami in Japan. (published 2319 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: AU OPTRONICS PINS HOPES ON SOLAR BUSINESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Taiwanese flat-panel maker \f28 \uc2 \f2 AU Optronics Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is pinning its hopes on the company's new solar business for a boost in its long-term growth prospects, as intensifying competition in the panel market and weak panel prices have weighed on its earnings. (published 0403 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par MALAYSIA TOP GLOVE 2Q NET DOWN 64% ON YEAR ON HIGH LATEX PRICES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Top Glove Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world's largest maker of latex gloves by volume, said Wednesday its fiscal second quarter earnings fell 64% from a year earlier owing to higher latex prices, a weak U.S. dollar and high-base effects. (published 0549 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CORNING: GLASS-MAKING \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 OPERATION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  UNAFFECTED BY SHIZUOKA QUAKE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Corning Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday its glass-making \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in Japan are running normally and there were no injuries or damages at its facilities in Shizuoka prefecture as a result of the earthquake Tuesday. (published 0135 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par THAI AIR CONTINUES FLIGHTS TO JAPAN DESPITE TRAFFIC VOLUME DROP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thai Airways International PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  continues to operate normal flights to and from Japan despite declines in passenger traffic volume following last week's earthquake and tsunami, President Piyasvasti Amranand said Wednesday. (published 0558 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK NEGARA 2010 NET PROFIT IDR4.1 TLN VS IDR2.48 TLN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 PT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Indonesia\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Wednesday it posted a net profit of IDR4.1 trillion in 2010, a 65% jump from IDR2.48 trillion a year earlier, supported by non-interest income and lower provisioning costs. (published 0627 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GRAINCORP REPORTS NO SHIPPING DELAYS YET FROM JAPAN DISASTERS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian exporter and logistics provider \f28 \uc2 \f2 GrainCorp Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday it hasn't yet experienced any delays to its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a result of the massive earthquake and tsunami that damaged some ports in northeastern Japan on Friday. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SIAM COMMERCIAL BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  KEEPS 2011 LENDING GROWTH TARGET AT 10%-12% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Siam Commercial Bank PCL\f28 \uc2 \f2  maintains its 2011 lending growth target at 10%-12% but expects to beat the target helped by strong demand for loans, President Kannikar Chalitaporn said Wednesday. (published 0526 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AIR INDIA FORMS FOUR-MEMBER PANEL TO EXAMINE PAY PARITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 16-03-11 0702GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Air India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . constituted an independent panel to study employees' pay parity of the merged national carrier after the federal Civil Aviation Ministry approved the proposal late Tuesday. (published 0339 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par OZ MINERALS: TAX OFFICE RULES THAT A$388 MILLION CAPITAL RETURN WON'T BE TAXED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A proposed A$388 million return of capital by \f28 \uc2 \f2 OZ Minerals Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . won't be taxable, according to a ruling by the Australian Taxation Office, the copper miner said Wednesday. (published 0535 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: ASIAN SHARES MOSTLY HIGHER; TOKYO SHARES UP, MOOD CAUTIOUS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mostly higher Wednesday, with the Tokyo market rebounding although it pared its morning gains as radiation levels again spiked at an earthquake-damaged nuclear complex. (published 0503 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 2ND UPDATE: JAPAN EDANO: RADIATION LEVELS SPIKED AT NUCLEAR PLANT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top government spokesman said Wednesday that radiation levels had again spiked at a smoking, quake-hit nuclear plant, but said there was no need to expand the evacuation area around the plant based on current data. (published 0600 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SK INNOVATION: TO HELP JX ENERGY WITH OIL, OIL PRODUCTS SUPPLY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 SK Innovation\f28 \uc2 \f2 , formerly known as SK Energy, said Wednesday it has held talks with Japan's JX Energy on ways to cooperate to ensure energy supplies in the country following the devastating earthquake and tsunami. (published 0545 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDONESIA COULD SHIP 59 EXTRA LNG CARGOES TO JAPAN -OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia could ship an additional 59 liquefied natural gas cargoes to Japan this year if the country requires more supply for electricity generation, after a massive earthquake last week shut down its nuclear power plants, a government official said Wednesday. (published 0336 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: AUSTRALIA GRAIN EXPORTER REPORTS DISRUPTION FROM JAPAN DISASTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Of Australia's major grain exporters, only \f28 \uc2 \f2 Cooperative Bulk Handling Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has reported any disruption to its shipping \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as a result of Friday's devastating earthquake and tsunami in northeastern Japan. (published 0510 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIA GOVERNMENT ORDERS JAPAN FOOD IMPORTS SCREENING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India will start screening any food items imported from Japan for possible contamination, the government said in a statement late Tuesday, amid growing fears over radiation leaks from a troubled nuclear plant in the quake-hit country. (published 0354 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA STEPS UP RADIATION VIGILANCE AMID JAPAN CRISIS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese authorities said Wednesday they were stepping up checks of incoming travelers and goods for possible radiation contamination as Japan's quake-triggered nuclear crisis escalated. (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par PALADIN ENERGY SAYS EVENTS IN JAPAN WILL EXACERBATE SUPPLY SITUATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Uranium producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Paladin Energy Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Wednesday the medium- and long-term outlook for nuclear power remains positive and recent events in Japan should exacerbate the uranium supply situation and put the company in an even better position in terms of global demand. (published 0531 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CHINA MINISTRY: 2011 SOYBEAN ACREAGE MAY FALL 11%; COTTON UP 5.4% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's soybean acreage this year may fall 11% from a year earlier while cotton acreage may rise 5.4%, the Ministry of Agriculture said. (published 0129 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: CHINESE FARMERS PLAN TO GROW MORE GRAIN, COTTON THIS YEAR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese farmers plans to plant more corn, rice and cotton this year in response to Beijing's supportive policies and high prices, the Ministry of Agriculture said. (published 0324 GMT) [ 16-03-11 0702GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110316e73g000f8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
