\par\par \b \uc2 FOCUS: Yen At Crossroads As BOJ Pumps In Cash\b0\par\par\uc2 835 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 16:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 -- Anticipated repatriation flows supporting yen\par \par \uc2 -- BOJ floods money market in expansionary move\par \par \uc2 -- \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  signals willingness to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken yen\par \par \uc2 -- Comparisons with yen effect from Kobe earthquake debatable\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Siva Sithraputhran \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 LONDON (Dow Jones)--The yen is weathering the devastating earthquake that hit Japan Friday remarkably well, supported by expectations that Japanese companies and citizens holding assets abroad will send back cash but the Bank of Japan's move to flood the interbank market with money is proving to be a crucial counterbalance.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The push and pull of these factors are keeping the yen stable for now. After the earthquake, the dollar first weakened against the yen, reaching Y80.60 earlier Monday, a level not seen since November 2010. But a raft of measures from the Bank of Japan to help put the economy on a better footing has helped the dollar drift higher to levels around Y82.00.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yen's exchange rate is crucial for Japan, because a strong yen will erode the competitiveness of the country's exports at a time when it is needed most.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 At 1246 GMT, the dollar was trading at Y81.23 while the euro was at Y114.20.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While expectations for repatriated funds are running high, at least among shorter-term traders, whether they will actually arrive from abroad remains to be seen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We don't see any evidence of that yet," said Ken Dickson, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investment director at Standard Life.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Looking at yen seasonality over the last four to five years, there is no discernible trend leading up to the Japanese fiscal year end. Repatriation flows do not look very strong," he said, adding that he isn't certain that the current circumstances will change the game.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 He expects the yen to weaken further out as Japan's budget deficit balloons and as the Bank of Japan keeps monetary policy loose for an extended period.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  Corporates & Markets said in a note to clients that some Japanese holders of oversees assets may well repatriate funds.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Due to its large portfolio of investments abroad [at the end of 2009: Y262 trillion, almost EUR2 trillion] repatriation is a strong argument for the yen. Insurance companies, in particular, will repatriate foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  investment so as to be able to cover demand arising from the catastrophe," they said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In the meantime, Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has acted decisively Monday, doubling the size of its asset-purchase program and pouring a record Y15 trillion into money markets to ease liquidity concerns. That came after the BOJ pumped a record amount of cash into money markets, offering same-day funds through three separate \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which effectively serve to make funding available immediately rather than after a settlement period.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts said these moves will be negatives for the yen. In newly issued forecasts Monday, the bank expects the dollar to rise gradually against the yen through the course of the year, from Y83 at the end of the first quarter to Y84, Y86 and Y92 in the next three quarters respectively.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Also Monday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market got an oblique warning from Japanese Finance Minister Yoshihiko Noda who said that the country's authorities will monitor yen levels. A more direct statement from a senior official at the Finance Ministry warned of the possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In light of these developments, Mark Hewlett, partner at Anello Asset Management said: "It may be worth waiting few days, even a few weeks before making a decision [on the yen]."\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But he noted that the Kobe earthquake of 1995 had driven the yen higher by 20%.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The comparison with the Kobe earthquake has been inevitable. But analysts are divided on just how far the comparison can be used as a guide for now and whether it should be used as a basis to buy the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "It may be too early to discuss how much damage was done to housing and infrastructure, but we suspect it could match that of the Great Hanshin Earthquake in 1995," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Kiichi Murashima said in a note to clients.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas\f28 \uc2 \f2  argued that circumstances have changed since 1995 and that it may be premature to expect the yen to rise by such a large amount.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 They said the insurance bill this time around will be larger while Japan now has a debt level of 200% of GDP, which in turn raises questions about funding any program to boost the economy. Additionally, the BOJ is now playing a much bigger role and the accommodative stance will weigh on the yen.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "At the highs of its 2004/2005 quantitative easing, the BOJ expanded its balance sheet by Y35 trillion, which resulted in the dollar rallying from 105 yen to 124 yen," the BNP analysts said.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Siva Sithraputhran, Dow Jones Newswires; +44-20-7842-9462; siva.sithraputhran@dowjones.com [ 14-03-11 1539GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 4135  \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020110314e73e0001s\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
