\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: Aussie CDS Fair Given Japan Quake - Deutsche\b0\par\par\uc2 1,707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 00:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2327 GMT [Dow Jones] Aussie iTraxx CDS index opens little changed early around 109-110 bps, close to fair value, say \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  strategists. "We think the index is currently fair at 110 basis points, reflecting the very negative news flow out of Japan over the weekend but the positive European announcement over the weekend." (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 2326 GMT [Dow Jones] QBE (QBE.AU) CDS are fairly valued around 130 bps given their estimate of net claims after Japan's earthquake, says a \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  credit strategist; QBE CDS were last at 128-133 bps. QBE estimates net claims for the quake around US$125 million. "The majority of the estimated net claims from the Japan disaster will come from the relatively low exposures in the company's reinsurance, marine and energy \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Deutsche says. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2325 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/JPY is at 81.45 after briefly touching a four-month-low of 80.60; many investors say it's possible that speculators may try to push the pair down to its record low of 79.75. Still, \uc2 Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's general manager of investment marketing division Jun Kato says the pair should find firm support at 80.50 because the after-quake repatriation talk that's been pressuring down the pair is groundless. A senior fund manager at a major Japanese life insurance firm says less than 10% of his whole portfolio is in non-Japanese assets. A senior government official says