\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: AUD/USD Fair Value Now At 0.9830 - NAB\b0\par\par\uc2 1,443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 22:50\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2150 GMT [Dow Jones] Fair value for the AUD/USD is now at 0.9830 mainly due to the decline in industrial metals prices and risk appetite, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Australia Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist John Kyriakopoulos. "We'll need to see a rebound in metals prices, otherwise AUD/USD will drift lower, especially with no important Australian economic reports due this week." Pair last 1.0127. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 2147 GMT [Dow Jones] There's plenty of event risk for \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in the coming week, says NAB chief strategist John Kyriakopoulos. The U.S. Fed rate decision Wednesday is top of the bill, though policy makers aren't expected to change their language much. "A better performing U.S. economy will again be acknowledged by the Fed but this will be tempered by reference to considerable slack remaining in the labor market," Kyriakopoulos says. After that traders are expecting a rate hike by the ECB next month, so euro-zone inflation Wednesday will be crucial. EUR/USD last 1.3959. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2144 GMT [Dow Jones] \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders are waiting to see how the BOJ responds to the earthquake and whether it expands its quantitative easing or boosts liquidity, says \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2  chief \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist John Kyriakopoulos. "Should Japan significantly increase both quantitative easing and government spending, then we'd expect the JPY to start to weaken." USD/JPY last 81.895. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2139 GMT [Dow Jones] Japan's earthquake appears to be localised in its impact and may not trigger a fresh bout of global risk aversion, says RBS \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Greg Gibbs. "It doesn't lend itself to a global risk aversion event." Notes Japan isn't a big supplier of commodities and the manufactured goods can be replaced by other countries and if anything could lead to demand for energy or commodities. "That creates stimulus for other countries, so I don't necessarily see this as a derailing global growth story." AUD/USD last 1.0139. (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2138 GMT [Dow Jones] Given the early price action in USD/JPY, there's an increasing risk that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will look to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says RBS \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Greg Gibbs. "You would certainly anticipate authorities in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be more inclined to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  than they would otherwise," he says. A slowing of economic activity after Friday's earthquake and the higher JPY will hurt in the near term, before reconstruction efforts boost demand, he says. USD/JPY last 81.80. Gibbs says a drop toward 80.00 will likely trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (enda.curran@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 2122 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/JPY cross will likely fall towards 80.00 in a session where risk off will dominate, with some chance the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  looks to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , says CBA \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Joseph Capurso. "It's certainly not a good environment for risk \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." USD