\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  COLUMN-Yield spreads set to push euro/yen higher\b0\par\par\uc2 821 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2011\par 15:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 -- Jeremy Boulton is an \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market analyst for Reuters. The opinions expressed are his own --\par \par \uc2 By Jeremy Boulton\par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 7 (Reuters) - The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's more hawkish outlook and the risk-on bias in equities, that has supported stocks as Middle East and North Africa tension has risen, should lift the euro to new heights versus the yen.\par \par \uc2 Buyers of euro/yen <EUR/JPY=> are chasing the improved returns envisaged since hawkish comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet last week.\par \par \uc2 His emphasis on the need for "strong vigilance" on inflation has been taken as a signal that the ECB will instigate a tightening cycle this year [ID:nLDE7220KJ].\par \par \uc2 Up to 75 basis points of euro zone rate hikes are priced in by December. [ECBWATCH]\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, despite some progress towards beating deflation, the Bank of Japan is sticking with its ultra-easy monetary policy [ID:nTOE726016]. The market sees no probability of any change in official rates this year. [BOJWATCH]\par \par \uc2 Indeed, the Bank of Japan is expected to be the last major \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to move towards higher interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The spread between German Bunds and Japanese government bonds has reacted accordingly, with German two-year debt yielding an additional 25 bps over its Japanese equivalent since March 3, when Trichet said the ECB may hike rates next month. [ID:nLDE7220KJ] <^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\par \par \uc2 Graphic on Japanese/German bond spread and euro/yen\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://link.reuters.com/hun48r"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://link.reuters.com/hun48r}}}\uc2  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^>\par \par \uc2 Euro/yen has rallied around 3 percent as a result of the shift in thinking at the ECB, at one time extending beyond a series of key peaks made in the latter half of 2010 between 115 and 116 yen.\par \par \uc2 That is seen as a bullish signal with potential in the medium-term for a move towards 125.00 yen.\par \par \uc2 Fiscal year end in Japan may also work to pivot flows in euro/yen.\par \par \uc2 The run-up to the March 31 fiscal year end traditionally sees exporters more actively buying yen and Japanese firms repatriating funds to dress up balance sheets. Thereafter Japanese investment managers receive fresh funds and the yen is more often than not sold as investors seek better yields.\par \par \uc2 However, in most recent trade euro/yen has retained a bid tone in the face of heavy exporter sales, and when Japanese investment managers enter the fray in April, they may see both a positive price action, and an enhanced carry, as reasons to buy.\par \par \uc2 Given Japanese insurance companies control assets equivalent to the size of Brazil's economy ($1.6 trillion), their investment decisions will be a key factor for future trade.\par \par \uc2 There is also a more pro-risk environment in evidence. On one hand fears about the euro zone periphery, although still elevated, have been put on the back burner in favour of a focus on the likelihood of higher euro zone interest rates.\par \par \uc2 The fact that both the Japanese [IF:nTOE726011] and Chinese governments opted to buy into European debt in a show of solidarity with Europe and the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is also likely to influence Asian bond fund managers in April.\par \par \uc2 Investment managers will also be guided by the performance of global equities and the global economic outlook. In this respect, both factors looks set to guide a risk on sentiment, that itself should underpin trades like euro/yen.\par \par \uc2 Stock markets have proved resilient to crisis in the euro zone and the escalation of MENA tensions. The MSCI world index [ID:.MIWD00000PUS] is up around 4.5 percent this year, the Dow Jones Index <.DJI> around 5 percent.\par \par \uc2 Such resilience has turned investors increasingly bullish, as has the fact that China's economy is holding up in the face of tighter monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 U.S. data has also shown improvement with the jobless rate dropping to 8.9 percent, but Federal Reserve monetary policy remains ultra-accommodative.\par \par \uc2 CARRY TRADES\par \par \uc2 This is fuel for a more pro-risk outlook in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, and for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders this environment would usually entail a greater focus on carry trades and a search for higher yields.\par \par \uc2 The yield for euro/yen longs is expected to increase by 75 percent by year end, and given the euro offers liquidity only second to that of the dollar, all investors, not just Japanese investment managers, will see better cause to go long.\par \par \uc2 There is also a more bullish technical background for euro/yen which on March 4 broke to a 116 yen, its highest since the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's September \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Prior to September, the last significant move involved the euro's sharp May decline from levels above 125.00. Some see potential for a retracement of this move in the medium term.\par \par \uc2 Buyers of euro/yen could be set to gain both through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation and in anticipation of rising yields.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-EUROYEN (\b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  COLUMN)   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110311e7380013i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
