\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF Data Shows No  \highlight22\uc2 FX Intervention \highlight\uc2  Jan 28-Feb 24\b0\par\par\uc2 123 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2011\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in the Jan. 28-Feb. 24 period, data released from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed Monday.\par \par \uc2 The outcome was expected by market participants.\par \par \uc2 The new data confirm that the MOF has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since Sept. 15, when the ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in more than six years in an effort to tame the soaring yen.\par \par \uc2 Monday's data cover trades settled in February. Trades in the spot market are settled after two business days.\par \par \uc2 -By Kosaku Narioka, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2784; kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com [ 28-02-11 1005GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110228e72s000ug\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
