\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Jan foreign reserves at $1.092 trln\b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Februar 2011\par 00:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  (For more stories on the Japanese economy, click [ID:nECONJP])\par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Feb 7 (Reuters) - Japan's foreign reserves declined to $1.092 trillion at the end of January, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday.\par \par \uc2  Japanese authorities spent 2.1249 trillion yen ($25.85 billion) on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the month to Sept. 28 last year, its first foray into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in over six years, but subsequently stayed out of the market at least until Jan. 27, ministry data has shown.\par \par \uc2  Japan's foreign reserves, the world's second-biggest after China's, hit a record high of $1.118 trillion at the end of October, a month after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the yen's rise from hurting its crucial export sector.\par \par \uc2  JAPAN OFFICIAL RESERVE ASSETS (in billion dollars)\par \par \uc2            END-JAN     END-DEC    END-NOV    YEAR AGO\par \par \uc2  TOTAL   1,092.980   1,096.185   1,101.031   1,053.070\par \par \uc2  To view the full tables, go to the MOF website at: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.mof.go.jp/english/e1c006.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.mof.go.jp/english/e1c006.htm}}}\uc2  (Reporting by Kaori Kaneko; Editing by Edwina Gibbs)                          \par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/RESERVES|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|NAT|U   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110206e726000h1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
