\par\par \b \uc2 Ex-BOJ official to take post at UAE  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 211 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2011\par 04:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 1 (Reuters) - A former senior Bank of Japan official is to work for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the United Arab Emirates, underscoring increasingly close bilateral relationships.\par \par \uc2 Masaru Tanaka, who held key positions at the BOJ such as in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  division overseeing \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  around 2000 and in the banking inspection department during \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's financial system crisis, resigned from the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Jan. 31.\par \par \uc2 Tanaka said he will be a "senior reviewer" at the UAE \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and his work will likely be related to banking inspections, possibly intended to draw on Japan's expertise in dealing with non-performing loans.\par \par \uc2 It will be the first time a former BOJ employee has worked for the UAE \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Tanaka said.\par \par \uc2 The UAE is the second-biggest oil supplier to Japan after Saudi Arabia, accounting for 20.4 percent of Tokyo's oil imports in 2010, after Saudi Arabia's 28.8 percent.\par \par \uc2 Japan has been stepping up ties with the UAE to help Japanese companies' oil production there. [ID:nLDE6A71SH] (Reporting by Chikako Mogi; Editing by Michael Watson)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-UAE/|LANGEN|J|ABN|E|RBN|M|D|GFN|MD|O|OIL|RNP|DNP|PEN   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020110201e7210004x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
