\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW: Former Japan  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Official Says Yen To Weaken\b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2011\par 07:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2011 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds Utsumi's comments on JGBs and BOJ.)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Takashi Mochizuki \par    Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--European officials should be able to bring about a happy ending to the region's sovereign debt problems and that should decrease demand for the yen in turn, a former top Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said.\par \par \uc2 Noting that it was purely investors looking for a safe haven that pushed the yen to a 15-year-high against the greenback last year, what lies ahead for the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a downtrend, said Makoto Utsumi, who was Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs between 1989 and 1991.\par \par \uc2 "What I can say for sure is the yen has hit its peak," he said in a recent interview with Dow Jones Newswires. "The dollar may trade in a Y85-Y90 range by June and may reach Y95 by the year-end, and the euro may rise to a Y115-125 range in the coming six months."\par \par \uc2 It's unclear how much his remarks reflect the feelings of the people in power in Tokyo, but his opinion adds to a growing view that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't stage another \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As of 0450GMT, the dollar was at Y82.16 and the euro was at Y112.58.\par \par \uc2 Market participants remain cautious about European debt problems and many of them say the issue should continue to weigh on the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and demand for the safe-haven yen will stay intact. But Utsumi, who has close friendships with top European officials and awarded France's Legion Honneur Commandeur in 2007, was sanguine on the outlook, adding its break below the key $1.30-mark appears unlikely for now.\par \par \uc2 "It's impossible that European nations will let the euro die, and we will see proof," he said, adding the recently-established fund in the euro zone was an example of the region's efforts.\par \par \uc2 Also weighing on the yen are expectations that yields will remain higher globally because the Federal Reserve isn't likely to compile another package of monetary easing measures, Utsumi said. When yields rise, the yen often bears the brunt because Japan's yields are lower than those of major rivals.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan is currently pumping massive liquidity into the market in an attempt to keep longer-term interest rates at low levels. But Utsumi criticized the maneuver, saying a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone can't fight this type of global trend.\par \par \uc2 "No matter what the BOJ does, Japan's yields can't be exempt once yields start to rise globally," said Utsumi, who heads the Japan Credit Rating Agency now.\par \par \uc2 A higher yield is often said a bad thing for Japan because it increases funding costs and makes the nation's fiscal rehabilitation more difficult. Utsumi, on the other hand, said it's not.\par \par \uc2 Japanese banks are main holders of Japan's debt, and because a lot of people park their money in bank accounts, and higher yields should fuel household income and consumption. That in turn increases the nation's tax income and can cancel most of the increase in debt serving costs, Utsumi noted.\par \par \uc2 "Japan should welcome higher yields," he said.\par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Mochizuki, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-6269-2782; takashi.mochizuki@dowjones.com [ 27-01-11 0643GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020110127e71r000gs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoa