\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ ASIA DAILY  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  OUTLOOK: Predicted Ranges, Themes-2-\b0\par\par\uc2 908 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Januar 2011\par 01:13\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 USD/JPY to consolidate with risks skewed higher amid improved USD sentiment (ICE spot dollar index last 79.43 vs 79.21 early Tuesday) after surprise 0.7% rise in U.S. November factory-goods orders (vs forecast for 0.1% decline), minutes from U.S. Federal Reserve''''s latest monetary policy meeting showing \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  more optimistic on economic growth outlook and expects dollar to rise higher than previously forecast. USD/JPY also underpinned by USD demand for import settlements, lingering fear of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF JPY-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But USD/JPY topside limited by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  exporter sales. No strong cue for JPY-funded carry trades from Wall Street as U.S. stocks closed narrowly mixed overnight (DJIA up 0.18%, S&P off 0.13%). Data focus: 2350 GMT Japan December monetary base, 1315 GMT U.S. December ADP national employment report, 1500 GMT U.S. December ISM non-manufacturing PMI, 1800 GMT Fed''''s Hoenig speaks.\par \par \uc2  USD/JPY daily chart positive-biased as stochastics bullish at oversold, negative MACD histogram bars contracting. Resistance at 82.28 (yesterday''''s high, just beneath previous base set Dec. 7); breach would expose upside to 82.62 (55-day moving average), then 82.97 (Dec. 27 high) and 83.15 (Dec. 24 high). Support at 81.61 (yesterday''''s low); breach would temper near-term positive outlook, targeting 81.44 (hourly chart), then 80.93 (Monday''''s low), 80.50 (Nov. 9 low) and 80.21 (15-year low set Nov. 1).\par \par \uc2 EUR/USD to consolidate with risks skewed lower. Pair undermined by improved USD sentiment, contagion from weaker commodity-linked \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , lingering worries that euro zone sovereign debt crisis will intensify this year; surprise rise in German unemployed by 3,000 in December (vs forecast for 13,000 drop). But EUR/USD losses tempered by EUR demand on rebounding EUR/AUD cross; higher-than-expected euro area inflation of 2.2% in December (vs 2.0% forecast) which above ECB''''s target of 2.0% for first time in 2 years. Data focus: 0855 GMT German December services PMI, 0900 GMT euro-zone December services PMI & composite PMI, 1000 GMT euro-zone November PPI, October new industrial orders. EUR/USD daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics turning bearish near overbought. Support at 1.3289 (yesterday''''s low); breach would target 1.3248 (Monday''''s low), then 1.3210 (Thursday''''s low), 1.3081 (Dec. 29 low, matching 200-day moving average), 1.3070 (Dec. 27 low) and 1.3053 (Dec. 23 low). Resistance at 1.3378 (hourly chart), then at 1.3433 (yesterday''''s high); breach would expose upside to 1.3483 (55-day moving average), then 1.3500 (Dec. 14 reaction high) and 1.3786 (Nov. 22 reaction high).\par \par \uc2 NZD/USD to trade with risks skewed lower. Pair undermined by improved USD sentiment, softer commodity prices, worries over weaker China economic growth and euro-zone sovereign debt crisis. But NZD/USD losses tempered by NZD-USD yield gap. NZD/USD daily chart mixed as MACD bullish, but stochastics falling from overbought. Support at 0.7638 (yesterday''''s low); breach would target 0.7604 (55-day moving average), then 0.7536 (Dec. 29 low) and 0.7470 (100-day moving average). Resistance at 0.7693 (hourly chart), then at 0.7741 (yesterday''''s high); breach would expose upside to 0.7784 (Monday''''s high), then 0.7813 (Thursday''''s high), 0.7835 (Nov. 22 reaction high) and 0.7872 (Nov. 11 high).\par \par \uc2 USD/CHF to trade with risks skewed higher. Pair supported by improved USD sentiment, fears of SNB''''s CHF-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; CHF sales on rebounding EUR/CHF cross. Daily chart positive-biased as stochastics rising from oversold; negative MACD histogram bars contracting, bullish parabolic stop-and-reverse signal hit at 0.9468 yesterday. Resistance at 0.9516 (yesterday''''s high); breach would target 0.9532 (Dec. 29 high), then 0.9605 (Dec. 28 high), 0.9645 (Dec. 17 high) and 0.9662 (Dec. 23 reaction high). Support at 0.9429 (hourly chart); breach would expose downside to 0.9322-0.9316 band (yesterday''''s low-Monday''''s low), then 0.9301 (Friday''''s record low) and psychological 0.9200.\par \par \uc2 AUD/USD to trade lower. Pair undermined by concerns over adverse economic impact of Queensland''''s huge floods, improved USD sentiment, softer commodity prices (CRB spot index ended down 5.29 yesterday at 327.73), worries over euro-zone sovereign debt problems and slower China economic growth as Beijing tightens policy to combat inflation. But AUD/USD losses tempered by AUD-USD interest rate differential. Data focus: 0100 GMT Australia December VFACTS vehicle sales. AUD/USD daily chart negative-biased as spot broke below uptrend support line from Dec. 1 low of 0.9535 (now at 1.0146); stochastics falling from overbought; positive MACD histogram bars contracting; bearish parabolic stop-and-reverse signal hit at 1.0076 yesterday. Support at 1.0025 (yesterday''''s low); breach would target 0.9980 (Dec. 27 low), then 0.9948 (Dec. 22 low), 0.9915 (55-day moving average) and 0.9828 (Dec. 16 reaction low). Resistance at 1.0108 (hourly chart), then at 1.0146 and 1.0171 (yesterday''''s high); breach would expose upside to 1.0223 (Monday''''s high), then 1.0253 (Friday''''s post-float high).\par \par \uc2 -0-\par \par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2011 \uc2 Dow Jones & Company, Inc\uc2 . \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020110106e7150005n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley