\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/TWD Down; Tipped To Fall Below 29.00 In 2011\b0\par\par\uc2 1,264 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2010\par 09:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0842 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/TWD is at 30.217, recouping most of its losses after touching a fresh 13-year low of 29.080 earlier from 30.367 late Wednesday. Two traders say the pair rose suddenly during the last 15 minutes of the onshore trading session, which ends at 0800 GMT, after unidentified state-owned banks executed a few trades between themselves above 30.00. One of the traders says the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appears to remain very determined to keep a lid on the TWD, but in the onshore session, it will likely fall below 29.00 early next year unless the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rolls out drastic new policies against hot money flows. (aries.poon@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0840 GMT [Dow Jones] Yield spreads between peripheral euro-zone government bonds and 10-year bunds are mostly a touch higher. The Greek 10-year spread over bunds is up 6 bps at 949 bps, Ireland is 1.8 bps higher at 608.9 bps, Spain is 4 bps higher at 247.7 bps. Portugal is unchanged at around 363 bps. The spread between Italian 10-year bonds and bunds is up 5.7 bps at 187 bps, ahead of Thursday's Italian auction. (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0839 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/PHP is lower as a stream of remittances from overseas Filipinos continue to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of buying (the USD) to stem the PHP's rise, say local bank traders. The pair is at 43.84 in heavy volume vs 43.86 late Wednesday. Traders say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have bought more than $200 million near 43.80-43.84 late in the session. Next year, "the BSP will continue to be on its foot to temper the peso's strength," says one trader. The pair is expected to trade in a 43.70-44.00 band Monday. The PHP has gained 5.1% vs the USD since the start of 2010. (rhea.sandique-carlos@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0835 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/MYR is lower late at 3.0820 from 3.0880 late Wednesday, with \uc2 Bank Negara Malaysia\uc2  suspected of supporting the pair at these levels to stem declines. Two local traders say Bank Negara was suspected of buying USD at 3.0810 and 3.0820 to support the greenback. The pair's decline is in line with most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . For next week, 3.0810 is tipped as the major support level, one of the trader says. He adds, "For 2011, the ringgit is likely to continue to strengthen against the dollar," on the back of continued local economic growth and foreign-fund inflows. He says the pair could end 2011 between 2.9000 and 3.0000. (ankur.relia@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0823 GMT [Dow Jones] The sharp stop-driven selloff in EUR/CHF has pushed the Swiss franc up across the board. USD/CHF slumped to another all-time low of 0.9371, GBP/CHF an all-time low of 1.4550 and CHF/JPY the day's high of 86.17. EUR/CHF now trades at 1.2445 from a fresh all-time low of 1.2398. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0820 GMT [Dow Jones] Sticky inflation amid rising commodity prices and high food prices could halt Indian equity markets rise in 2011. "High food inflation has morphed into a structural issue now as rising urban and rural incomes continue to put upward pressure on food prices with supply constraints and underinvestment in the food supply chain limiting the supply-side response," says Nomura Securities. Besides, the house says other factors like crude oil prices, expensive valuations, tight liquidity affecting corporate growth and the return of political risk will be on foreign investor radars. (john.kumar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0818 GMT [Dow Jones] March gilts are up 0.62 at 118.48 and the 10-year gilt yields 3.499%, down from 3.574% Wednesday afternoon. The healthy response to an auction of 7-year U.S. Treasurys Wednesday is supporting European sovereign bonds amid low year-end volumes. "It's very quiet, but Treasurys should be able to move us a bit," says one strategist, adding the other major event of the day will be an auction of Italian government debt. "After that has cleared, we should be finished for the year." (mark.brown@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0817 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/CHF slumps to a fresh all-time low of 1.2398. A dealer at a UK bank says the move was stop driven, with option barriers taken out at 1.2440 and 1.2400, along with stops at 1.2425, 1.2420 and 1.2410. The cross has since bounced sharply to trade at 1.2437. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0811 GMT [Dow Jones]--The SNB will probably start raising rates in March, says \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2 . "While rates look inappropriate given the strength of the economy, the strength of the CHF has delayed the rate hikes," BNP says, referring to SNB's 3-Mos Libor target of 0.25%. BNP notes that SNB President recently sounded more on the hawkish side, talking about the declining deflation risk and pointing out that the overheating property market isn't compatible with loose monetary policy. (anita.greil@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0807 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD/JPY may fall sharply if Japanese retail investors exit their ballooning JPY short positions, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says. It adds, short JPY positions held by Japanese retail investors on the Tokyo Financial Exchange reached record levels Tuesday at Y507 billion, estimating this at 10% of the wider Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  margin trading market. JPY shorts against the USD are now "the most popular trade" among Japanese retail investors, likely due to the yen's historically strong level and possibility of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on further strengthening. However, it says the USD/JPY's recent falls made these retail investors vulnerable. With regulations allowing 50 times leverage, if stops are triggered in thin holiday trading, "the risk of a sudden yen-positive capitulation is very real." Still, the house re-affirms its 1-month and 3-month forecasts for the USD/JPY at 85.00. The pair is at 81.59.(kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0756 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/SEK is set to trade between 8.97 and 9.02 Thursday as Wednesday's range holds, says SEB. "Upside pressure is likely" after Tuesday's "bullish engulfing candle together with yesterday's downside spike", adds the bank. EUR/SEK trades at 8.9861.(charles.duxbury@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0752 GMT [Dow Jones] Hang Seng Bank expects China GDP growth to moderate to 8.5% in 2011 from an expected 10% in 2010 as a result of the recent accelerated pace of monetary tightening, the lingering of the sovereign debt problem in Europe and the fragile U.S. economic recovery. "With inflation and wages rising and signs of a rebound in property market activities emerging recently, more increases in the RRR and interest rates can be expected in coming months," the bank says in a report. It expects the PBOC to raise rates three times in early 2011 with a 25 bp hike each time. It also expects China inflation to hit 4.5% in 2011 from an expected 3.3% this year on higher food prices. (chester.yung@dowjones.com) [ 12-30-10 0342ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020101230e6cu0004k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
